Each rectangle is divided into $6$ equal parts. The whole rectangle contains $6$ shaded parts. Including the other $4$ shaded parts gives $6+4=10$ shaded parts in total.

The denominator stays $6$ because each part is still one of $6$ equal parts of a whole.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{4}{6} + 1 &= \frac{4}{6} + \frac{6}{6} \\
&= \frac{10}{6}
\end{aligned}
$$

Divide the numerator and denominator by their greatest common factor, $2$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{10}{6} &= \frac{10\div 2}{6\div 2} \\
&= \frac{5}{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

Grouping every $2$ small parts into one larger part gives the same shaded amount:

![The same amount regrouped into 3 equal parts per whole.](images/01/012eba9c2eb2750ea62fdd6ae2f698c4983717f1733973afa7de86c90d33bb7f.png)

Thus the answer is $\frac{5}{3}$, in lowest terms.

